# .memory-tree.conf — per-repo config for the memory-tree hygiene kit.
# Copy to your repo ROOT as `.memory-tree.conf` and EDIT. Sourced by every kit script
# (check-memory-hygiene.sh, gen_build_index.py, corpus_ids.py, gotchas.py, adopt-memory-tree.sh).
# Plain shell assignments only.

# Root folder of the structured memory tree, relative to the repo root.
MEMORY_ROOT=memory

# DISCIPLINES is a CLOSED ENUM of stream values, NOT a list of directories. The tree is FLAT: every
# build folder sits directly at $MEMORY_ROOT/builds/<slug>/ with no discipline segment and no date
# prefix, and which stream a spec served is declared in its own status header as
# `· streams <value>[+<value>]`. Space-separated, lowercase, [a-z-] only. Add a value only when
# content exists for it. REPLACE the example below with your project's streams.
DISCIPLINES="architecture deployment design"

# <enum value>:FAMILY — the id prefix for that stream's decisions (FAMILY-<slug>-<seq>), its backlog
# shard at $MEMORY_ROOT/backlog/<FAMILY>.md, and the optional FAMILY qualifier in a recording
# filename. There is ONE append-only $MEMORY_ROOT/DECISIONS.md for every family, grouped for
# reading. Space-separated, FAMILY uppercase [A-Z].
FAMILIES="architecture:ARCH deployment:DEPL design:DES"

# Old tree roots being migrated away from; blank when scaffolding fresh.
TOMBSTONE_ROOTS=""

# Spec-format ratchet (check 12). Set to the date you adopt the kit: every spec whose FILENAME date
# is >= this must follow $MEMORY_ROOT/TEMPLATE-SPEC.md — the status header, and for Tier-2 the ten
# canonical ## sections with no empty bodies. Older specs are grandfathered by filename date; never
# retrofit them. Blank = check 12 off. (§10 Reuse audit is separately date-gated by SPEC10_CUTOFF,
# which is a script default in check-memory-hygiene.sh and overridable from the environment.)
SPEC_FORMAT_CUTOFF=""

# Streams ratchet (check 12): specs dated >= this MUST carry `· streams <value>` in the status
# header. Set it strictly AHEAD of every committed spec's filename date at adoption, so no landed
# spec goes retroactively red — which also means your corpus does not exercise the required arm, and
# the kit's self-test carries explicit red/green fixtures for it instead.
STREAMS_CUTOFF=""
# Acceptance-witness ratchet (check 12): specs dated >= this must give every acceptance bullet a
# backticked token. Set it AHEAD of your corpus so nothing lands retroactively red. Blank = off.
SPEC_WITNESS_CUTOFF=""

# The document a session is pointed at before it touches code; check 16 derives the mandatory read
# path from it. Usually AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.
CHARTER="AGENTS.md"

# --- corpus_ids.py (checks 13-16). Every number below is MEASURED against YOUR corpus by
# --- `python memory-tree/corpus_ids.py --measure`, and NEVER inherited from another repo: a pin
# --- copied from a larger tree is either vacuous or permanently red. Blank turns its check off.
# --- Ship them blank, run --measure once the tree has content, and paste what it prints.
# Orphan ids: cited but never defined. Shrink-only once set.
ORPHAN_ID_PIN=""
# Dead repo-path citations in the present-tense corpus. Measure 0 on a fresh tree and it becomes a
# ratchet: the next unresolving citation reds until it is registered or repaired.
DEAD_PATH_PIN=""
# The charter's read path under MEMORY_ROOT, in bytes, plus headroom. One-sided: a session's
# mandatory reading is a budget, and a new binding doc spends from it visibly.
READ_PATH_CEILING=""
# Path prefixes that are NOT repo CONTENT (e.g. a worktree root). Resolution is `git ls-files`
# membership plus a prefix scan and never touches the filesystem, so a checkout LOCATION classifies
# identically on every node — which is why the answer is declared here rather than probed.
DEAD_PATH_EXCLUDE=""
# Read-path members deliberately under no byte cap, space-separated. Blank = every member is capped.
READ_PATH_WAIVER=""

# gotchas.py (checks 17-19): how many bug-class records under $MEMORY_ROOT/gotchas/ may be
# `universal: true`. A universal record is emitted on EVERY reviewer checklist, so this is budgeted
# rather than left to drift — a checklist nobody can finish is not a checklist. Blank = no budget.
# Unlike the pins above this is a POLICY CEILING you choose, not a measurement of your corpus — so
# it ships with a value rather than blank. Raise it in a commit that says why.
UNIVERSAL_BUDGET="3"

# memory-recall only (safe to delete if that kit is not adopted): the cache budget over the whole
# `<git-common-dir>/recall/cache/` tree, in megabytes. ABSENT = the kit's default (512 MB);
# BLANK = uncapped.
RECALL_CACHE_BUDGET_MB="512"

# Check 20 — ids duplicated INSIDE one row document. A POLICY refusal, not a measured-blank
# pin: ship it with a value. `row_grammar.py --emit-pin` prints the measured count for a tree
# that already has content.
ROW_DUPLICATE_PIN="0"
